METHOD NOTE — mutation without writing the shared tree
All mutations used Go's build overlay (`go test -overlay=<json>`): file
contents are substituted in the BUILD only, never on disk. Notably this
WORKS FOR go:embed too, which I did not assume — I proved it with a control
mutation before trusting any template result (see criterion 2/4). sha256sum
brackets every run:
  BASELINE and FINAL, identical:
    c4d7c13c655e48e49231d4c775a1abfb31d30c6b68a6d79996a2a1a9d1a9dbb8  internal/handlers/majorexpenses/handlers.go
    c806132e1b7ff479594d10dc75e6d122ecbbe07c3c5332ad4d2ec8e1d0221c77  internal/handlers/majorexpenses/handlers_test.go
    3c42afba1ad8e9040f1fd7a322875452c8ac8584a07b36a0e55f1fa51d458f87  web/templates/pages/major-expenses.html
My only write to the tree is this verdict file. No port used, no server
started, no write-mode git, no repo-root binary executed.

