-------------------------------------------------------------------------
FINDINGS (backlog — none block acceptance)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
F1 (test fragility, criterion "edit form renders the stored state checked"):
   the flagged-side assertion is `strings.Contains(flaggedSection, "checked")`
   over the WHOLE fragment, unanchored to the exclude_from_plan_sync input —
   unlike the unflagged-side assertion, which is correctly windowed to 200
   chars after the input's name/value match. Today it still discriminates
   (mutation T1 proves it), because the flagged fixture sets ONLY
   ExcludeFromPlanSync. But I characterised the fragility concretely rather
   than speculating: rendering an expense with IsInternalTransfer=true and
   ExcludeFromPlanSync=FALSE gives
     PROBE-SPEC section contains bare "checked" = true   (flag is FALSE)
     PROBE-SPEC windowed on the exclude input contains "checked" = false
   So the sibling transfer checkbox alone satisfies the unanchored form. The
   day someone adds IsInternalTransfer to that fixture, the assertion goes
   vacuous silently. One-line fix: window the flagged assertion the same way
   the unflagged one already is. Recording per the standing "a guard one
   element away is vacuous" rule; NOT a FAIL because the guard currently
   holds under mutation.
F2 (lane note, not mine to rule on): ACCESSIBILITY.md conformance — label
   association, keyboard reachability, visible focus, dark-mode class parity
   — is checker-a11y's bullet. Observation only: both new inputs are native
   `<input type="checkbox">` wrapped in a `<label>` (implicit association,
   matching the is_internal_transfer sibling, which uses no for/id either),
   and both carry the sibling's `focus:ring-indigo-500` and
   `dark:border-gray-600` classes verbatim. The edit-form instance uses
   `flex items-center gap-2 mt-1` and the create-form instance
   `flex items-start gap-2 text-xs`, each matching its own sibling's layout
   classes. I make no a11y ruling.
F3 (manifest hygiene): the manifest's "pre-existing whole-repo build break"
   note is stale (SY3 has landed; `go build ./...` is green). Worth a line in
   the run notes so a future reader does not chase a phantom break.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
All SY2 acceptance criteria in my lane are met, each on a quoted command's
output. Both forms carry exactly one correctly-named checkbox (counted
structurally against the sibling pattern, 2 and 2); the parse is shared by
construction through a single parseExpenseForm reached from both call sites;
the uncheck-clears-to-false round trip is proven on the update path and again
on raw stored JSON bytes; the rendered checked-state is proven per-expense in
BOTH directions by template mutations T1 and T3, validated by control
mutation T2 which first established that the overlay reaches go:embed; and
dropping the parse line fails tests on the unit, add and update paths. The
tree is byte-identical after every mutation.
